{"title":"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Coordbash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Coordbash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(simpler_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (simpler solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dbd99bf5f9a37b7ca89b0bccecdf413e1c8afd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a point at a distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525ff03c0dcdcfa6a7c9c46dc1a1474fef20d5cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + \\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> from the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of the circle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on the circle nearest to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. A line passing through the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the circle at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. The maximum possible area for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b10d643e22139a48a59762bbd05231dc39acd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3cec6689e7e99fee6744cef93887cfb24d78db52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a - b\\sqrt{c}}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947add5766b9f26f6dfe73d9425d87664416459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Coordbash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Coordbash)\">Solution 1 (Coordbash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Coordbash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f419c223647108f3ec0e7539c755b1fef842ed2d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import math; import olympiad; import graph; pair A, B, K, L; B = (sqrt(13), 0); A=(4+sqrt(13), 0); dot(B); dot(A);  draw(Circle((0,0), sqrt(13))); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, (0,0), S);label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW);label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, S); dot((0,0));    [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow we put the figure in the Cartesian plane, let the center of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74ce1e047c9e4ed59c485ca8fb37fd3088c6a4b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7d17b3ad45f95ef443e7fc2e651aa5ff0371ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B (\\sqrt{13},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/54554c9584ccbbf4bfda49329fba031a0f27dbff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(4+\\sqrt{13},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>The equation for Circle O is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4bd2f603fdf8008cecc19b4ff57587b62b7802.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, and let the slope of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7439149f594e9b8f42ef995654a5cf9d644b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKL$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, then the equation for line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7439149f594e9b8f42ef995654a5cf9d644b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKL$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b123741dd6ebdecf84c0ba8608c4977d6a9bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=k(x-4-\\sqrt{13})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Then we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dce30ffa550e8a2bb071434f4c63fe9277a40bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k^2+1)x^2-2k^2(4+\\sqrt{13})x+k^2\\cdot (4+\\sqrt{13})^2-13=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"431\" height=\"21\" />. According to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a>, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c40ec14360bfd44189f22a17558b22038f37599c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2=\\frac{2k^2(4+\\sqrt{13})}{k^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"189\" height=\"42\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42611a950c553b5dfa842a98209f626e752485bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1x_2=\\frac{(4+\\sqrt{13})^2\\cdot k^2-13}{k^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"219\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843269f5dc617ca20cc2ca334fd39e6ef70c1d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LK=\\sqrt{1+k^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{(x_1+x_2)^2-4x_1x_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"297\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Also, the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7097b70b28f5c53561a0e5a72a06d96bfeb90bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LK$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e04fa18d3a892286d9bebb5d3529ba531da46efe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k\\times \\sqrt{13}-(4+\\sqrt{13})\\cdot k}{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}=\\frac{-4k}{\\sqrt{1+k^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"284\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>So the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def918d1bd873a8d6b61f47fa582061c7ae912f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=0.5ah=\\frac{-4k\\sqrt{(16+8\\sqrt{13})k^2-13}}{k^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"316\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Then the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b321161c71f85bce78a702183c3090fbae1e8aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{104-26\\sqrt{13}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17ed9b219664a7d589e9319b16594d98816b149e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$104+26+13+3=\\boxed{146}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f419c223647108f3ec0e7539c755b1fef842ed2d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import math; import olympiad; import graph; pair A, B, K, L; B = (sqrt(13), 0); A=(4+sqrt(13), 0); dot(B); dot(A);  draw(Circle((0,0), sqrt(13))); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, (0,0), S);label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW);label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, S); dot((0,0));    [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p>Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00d16a122c17afcb2e71e4dc6dc03fda0210c17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\triangle OKL}{\\triangle BKL} = \\frac{OC}{BD} = \\frac{AO}{AB} = \\frac{4+\\sqrt{13}}{4}\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, to maximize area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b10d643e22139a48a59762bbd05231dc39acd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, we need to maximize area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd49c215fdaef9c0ea666922a26492d25dde25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/4273517b375629983d5a281e55038084fe3eb77b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle OKL = \\frac12 r^2 \\sin{\\angle KOL}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>So when area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd49c215fdaef9c0ea666922a26492d25dde25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is maximized, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83b51b388f0f13b86e8f2ac3004123491091513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KOL = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Eventually, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbeeabd682c746dbb6c1378a676aad5ab7041f44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle BKL=  \\frac12 \\cdot (\\sqrt{13})^2\\cdot(\\frac{4}{4+\\sqrt{13}})=\\frac{104-26\\sqrt{13}}{3}\\]\" width=\"388\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17ed9b219664a7d589e9319b16594d98816b149e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$104+26+13+3=\\boxed{146}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28simpler_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(simpler_solution)\">Solution 3 (simpler solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (simpler solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rather easier solution is presented in the Girls' Angle WordPress:\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://girlsangle.wordpress.com/2013/11/26/2013-aime-2-problem-10/\">http://girlsangle.wordpress.com/2013/11/26/2013-aime-2-problem-10/</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a23366a67bb9c3c217164999ddc2098b9deed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N,M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> les on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3d23869f7a418cd2cf0a8d3030ad37859aaa77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AL$\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12ec5fb5541f6a0820b01d9ae3afcb2e7e7fed6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM\\bot AL, ON\\bot AL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8923090889a231fa63ccbb16509e6336b0bdc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=h, ON=k,LN=KN=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"18\" /> We call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be85395df57104fbb96eb5953e6e9fb0361045b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{LON}=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> By similar triangle, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41085a77b75ce3f50fdb36c4aaa693be9336821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{h}{k}=\\frac{4}{4+\\sqrt{13}}, h=\\frac{4k}{4+\\sqrt{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"221\" height=\"44\" />. Then, we realize the area is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3dc69ddc66941b2dfbb1255acd1c60df1f322da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dh=d\\cdot \\frac{4K}{4+\\sqrt{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"137\" height=\"44\" /> As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601d2200760a17ff16676bebe41e0fad61d21813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha=\\frac{d}{\\sqrt{13}}, \\cos \\alpha=\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"209\" height=\"44\" />. Now, we have to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e6173042f9a54d49ba6c6fe2e7fd8d64ceecf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{52\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\alpha}{4+\\sqrt{13}}=\\frac{26\\sin 2\\alpha}{4+\\sqrt{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"202\" height=\"43\" />, which is obviously reached when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee396d3ed6a1412d6ec2a67a3b99b1db05a387e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha=45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b321161c71f85bce78a702183c3090fbae1e8aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{104-26\\sqrt{13}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"41\" /> leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7110d046bd9a944b2111b545e0c7e1ddb3efc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{146}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~bluesoul\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AIME-II-2013-10.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9f/AIME-II-2013-10.png/400px-AIME-II-2013-10.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"261\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/9f/AIME-II-2013-10.png/600px-AIME-II-2013-10.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/9f/AIME-II-2013-10.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let C and D be the base of perpendiculars dropped from points O and B to AK.  Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e860d74cd141ca5352128e66cf5f2c0198c629d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = h, OC = H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/45500c95e790d4d06615c4ea4b4425795bffb82d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle ABD \\sim \\triangle AOC \\implies \\frac {h}{H} = \\frac {4}{4 + \\sqrt{13}}.\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the base of  triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd49c215fdaef9c0ea666922a26492d25dde25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43e9e35b9227c87b9d65d305efd5f2163b882d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BKL \\implies \\frac {[BKL]}{[OKL]} = \\frac{h}{H} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"233\" height=\"45\" /> const <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" />\nThe maximum possible area for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b10d643e22139a48a59762bbd05231dc39acd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd49c215fdaef9c0ea666922a26492d25dde25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are at the same position of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd49c215fdaef9c0ea666922a26492d25dde25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OKL$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfbc9723ab9e5b88b0babed61c2428468ff886e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OK = OL = \\sqrt{13}\\implies \\max[\\triangle OKL] = \\frac {OK^2}{2} = \\frac {13}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>in the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822dde3c4a106365f704d7c95ea2654199245f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KOL = 90^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" /> It is possible – if we rotate such triangle, we can find position when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e60ccac3effd89e9e1929b74e1913fff9ef8ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f02ebd8fc5a5f597a23013d91e18c70c8242aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\max[\\triangle BKL] = \\max[\\triangle OKL] \\cdot \\frac {4}{4+\\sqrt{13}} = \\frac {26}{4+\\sqrt{13}} \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{146}}\\]\" width=\"495\" height=\"41\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II\" title=\"2013 AIME II\">2013 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017043538\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.092 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 494/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15389/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.607      1 -total\n 58.80%    7.413      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.56%    4.988      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki